// Quiz for CASCADE topic

::CASCADE::
The client needs to adjust the primary key of a parent record on a frequent basis, how should I construct my child tables to prevent data inconsistencies? {
~Use `ON DELETE CASCADE` with the foreign key reference to the parent record id.
~There is no need, SQL will automatically do this for me.
=Use `ON UPDATE CASCADE` with the foreign key reference to the parent record id.
~This is not possible
}

::CASCADE::
You want to remove a parent record that is referenced in several tables, but you're presented an error with the deletion "a foreign key constraint fails". 
How could you fix this so your previous command will work for any additional attempts at deleting a parent record in the future? {
~Update the child tables foreign key to be different than the one in the parent record
=Alter the child table foreign key to allow for deletion on cascade, using `ON DELETE CASCADE`
~Delete each record from the child tables
~This is not possible
}
